# Git Flow

This project follows classic [Git Flow](https://nvie.com/posts/a-successful-git-branching-model/).

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | Production releases only |
| `develop` | Integration / next release |
| `feature/*` | New work from `develop` → merge back into `develop` |
| `release/*` | Release prep from `develop` → merge into `main` and `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | Urgent fixes from `main` → merge into `main` and `develop` |

## Agent behavior

- Branch features from `develop`, never from `main`.
- Open feature PRs against `develop`.
- Promote to `main` only via `release/*` (or `hotfix/*`).
- After a release/hotfix merge to `main`, also merge back into `develop`.
- Do not push feature work directly to `main`.

## Before every `git push`

Always run locally (and fix failures) **before** any `git push`:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run format:check
```

- If lint fails: `npm run lint:fix`, then re-run `npm run lint`.
- If Prettier fails: `npm run format`, then re-run `npm run format:check`.
- Include any auto-fixed files in a commit before pushing.
- Do not push with known lint/format failures (Netlify `prebuild` will reject them).
